{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"almondy-aventurine-leonberger","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Observed during bug 941b-f049-5f29-4410's rebar-debug pass.\n\nAGENTS.md sets a target of 200-500 LOC per file and a **hard cap of 800**. The CI module-size\ngate that enforces it covers `src/rebar` only, so this file is over the cap without failing\nthe build.\n\n    932 tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py\n\nIt was 917 before 941b and is 932 after (941b removed the session-start field gate and the\n`_CAPABILITY_FIELD_CONFIRM_BUDGET_S` cap, and added the provisioning evidence that explains\nwhy). So 941b did not create the condition and did not meaningfully worsen it, but it also did\nnot fix it, and splitting it was out of that bug's scope.\n\nPer the module-size policy, a split must follow call-graph seams that already exist and must\nnot create files under 100 LOC. Candidate seams visible in the file today: the PAT\nmint/sweep/reclaim cluster (`jira_dc_pat`, `_leaked_harness_tokens`,\n`_sweep_leaked_harness_tokens`), and the scratch-project provisioning + teardown cluster\n(`_create_scratch_project`, `_assert_project_capabilities`, `_leaked_scratch_projects`,\n`_poll_until_404`). Both are already cohesive groups that call among themselves.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py` is at or under 800 LOC\n- [ ] the split follows an existing call-graph seam and creates no file under 100 LOC\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py` and `tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_provisioning.py`\n      still pass (both load the conftest by PATH, so a move must keep the loaded module's\n      surface intact)","id":"ccf6-a065-b1d6-4cf1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py is 932 LOC, over the 800 hard cap"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785913747238112001,"uuid":"a02a20f1-3776-40d0-8b60-2eb5c13fb83b"}